{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a leader of the County of Tripoli a Crusader state in the Holy Land. He was born in 1140 and died in 1187. Raymond was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was the sister of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem and King Amalric I of Jerusalem. \n\n## Early Life and Reign\n*Early Life* Raymond III was born in 1140. After his father's assassination in 1152 Raymond III succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. As he was still a minor his mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. \n\nRaymond III was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi in 1164 during the Battle of Harim. He was released in 1173 after being held captive for nearly a decade. During his captivity his stepfather Walter of Saint Omer acted as regent of Tripoli.\n\n## Military Campaigns and Politics\n*Reign and Military Campaigns* After his release from captivity Raymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was a leader of the faction opposed to King Guy of Lusignan. Raymond III was a cousin of King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem and was one of his closest advisors. \n\nIn 1180 Raymond III was appointed as regent for King Baldwin IV who was suffering from leprosy. He was also the bailli or regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. As regent Raymond III arranged the marriage of Princess Sibylla sister of King Baldwin IV to Baldwin of Ramla. However the King later changed his mind and married Sibylla to Guy of Lusignan.\n\n## Conflict with Guy of Lusignan and Death\n*Conflict and Death* The conflict between Raymond III and Guy of Lusignan continued until the death of King Baldwin IV in 1185. After the King's death Raymond III supported the claim of King Baldwin V to the throne. However Baldwin V died in 1186 and Guy of Lusignan became the King. \n\nThe conflict between Raymond III and Guy of Lusignan ultimately led to the Battle of Hattin in 1187. Raymond III played a significant role in the battle but the Crusader army was defeated. Raymond III died soon after the battle possibly due to illness or injury. He was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV Count of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.018178174272179604}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0003358753747306764}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0019338493002578616}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.20410853624343872}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.037504423409700394}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.468355655670166}, {"token": " leader", "logprob": -0.4783802628517151}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0011804286623373628}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.5829592943191528}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.03851732239127159}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.07893811166286469}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.25423097610473633}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.002687059575691819}, {"token": " Holy", "logprob": -0.07921182364225388}, {"token": " Land", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.003893771907314658}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.0006768796010874212}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0006051616510376334}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.018698494881391525}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.474083811044693}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.1271771788597107}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"